\caption{Observed writing-process trajectories.
Panel (a) shows the most frequent complete paths; panels (b) and (c) show transition counts for \condAgenticCogWriter\ and \condFixedOrder.
Our system mostly follows the same forward Planning--Translating--Reviewing progression as \condFixedOrder; returns to Translating are more common than returns to Planning, consistent with the small exploratory advantage of adaptive ordering.}

Observed departures from the common process path do not show a larger quality advantage.
Table~\ref{tab:trace-outcome} compares runs that complete exactly one planning--drafting--reviewing cycle with runs that take any other path and finds similar pairwise win rates against \condFixedOrder\ and \condSingleWriter.
Because the split is observational rather than randomized, it cannot establish whether a different path improves or worsens output.\footnote{See Appendix~\ref{app:process-behavior} for process, goal, and resource statistics.}
